Package: com.huhansibuxin.disablebgkeepalive
Name: DisableBgKeepalive
Depends: mobilesubstrate, ellekit
Version: 1.2.0
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Description: 禁用后台保活 (Disable Background Keepalive). Two jobs in one dylib.
 (1) Kill every iOS 16 runtime keepalive channel: beginBackgroundTask*, legacy
 VoIP setKeepAliveTimeout:, BGTaskScheduler, PKPushRegistry/VoIP,
 CLLocationManager, background fetch, CBCentralManager/CBPeripheralManager
 restore, NSURLSession background, HKHealthStore delivery, silent push. All are
 refused/short-circuited whenever the app is not in the foreground, so the
 system suspends it immediately after leaving (zero background CPU).
 (2) Auto-exit on any non-user-initiated launch: if the app is started or woken
 in the background by the system (location change, bluetooth change, background
 fetch, background URLSession, silent/remote push), it exits immediately. Only
 launches you start yourself (icon tap / notification tap) are allowed through.
 All waiting and killing happens on a background queue; the main thread is never
 blocked. For static UIBackgroundModes, run strip_bg_modes.sh on the target
 bundle id.
Maintainer: huhansibuxin
Author: huhansibuxin
Section: Tweaks
